my presentation is going to
be a little bit technical,

00:06:21.270 --> 00:06:23.500
but my-

00:06:23.500 --> 00:06:25.170
intention is, actually,

00:06:25.170 --> 00:06:29.790
to highlight the core-structures
of causal networks,

00:06:29.790 --> 00:06:34.790
and the main philosophical
reasoning there.

00:06:37.145 --> 00:06:38.367
I want to make the point,

00:06:38.367 --> 00:06:42.650
as an introduction, I
want to make this point,

00:06:42.650 --> 00:06:44.270
how far we can get, actually,

00:06:44.270 --> 00:06:46.813
with a mathematical, formal structure of-

00:06:48.140 --> 00:06:49.103
causation.

00:06:50.290 --> 00:06:52.470
This is the outline of my presentation,

00:06:52.470 --> 00:06:55.790
I know I'm not going to have enough time

00:06:55.790 --> 00:06:59.660
to go through all these
subjects in detail,

00:06:59.660 --> 00:07:04.610
but I think I will try to
communicate the main points.

00:07:04.610 --> 00:07:07.130
Let's start with the causal,

00:07:07.130 --> 00:07:09.860
with the structure of causal networks.

00:07:09.860 --> 00:07:13.990
So the main building-block
of a causal network,

00:07:13.990 --> 00:07:17.026
is the notion of a mechanism.

00:07:17.026 --> 00:07:19.083
And the mechanism is-

00:07:23.000 --> 00:07:26.030
basically, the idea is
that you have a function,

00:07:26.030 --> 00:07:31.030
so it's mathematical
object, f of X, Y is f of X,

00:07:31.060 --> 00:07:35.080
and then you allow for
disturbances of that function.

00:07:35.080 --> 00:07:37.710
So, this is the disturbance, U.

00:07:37.710 --> 00:07:41.410
Often, you have a model
where Y equals f of X,

00:07:41.410 --> 00:07:42.790
plus some disturbance,

00:07:42.790 --> 00:07:45.430
so that would be some
kind of additive noise,

00:07:45.430 --> 00:07:47.670
it can be multiplicative noise,

00:07:47.670 --> 00:07:50.950
but this version of it
is much more general,

00:07:50.950 --> 00:07:55.290
so the function itself
depends on the input, X,

00:07:55.290 --> 00:07:56.760
and the disturbance, U.

00:07:56.760 --> 00:08:00.023
So that's the most general
way to write down a-

00:08:01.210 --> 00:08:03.949
a mechanism, a deterministic mechanism.

00:08:03.949 --> 00:08:08.949
That actually has been already
considered in genetics,

00:08:09.350 --> 00:08:12.120
and in econometrics, social sciences,

00:08:12.120 --> 00:08:13.793
information theory, and so on.

00:08:14.980 --> 00:08:17.660
So, the idea is, that the disturbance,

00:08:17.660 --> 00:08:19.890
it's actually not observable,

00:08:19.890 --> 00:08:22.583
so what you observe is the X and Y.

00:08:23.810 --> 00:08:26.430
So let me, okay.

00:08:26.430 --> 00:08:29.570
Basically, you integrate
out the disturbance,

00:08:29.570 --> 00:08:31.483
and as outcome Y,

00:08:32.584 --> 00:08:35.230
you get a distribution of points.

00:08:35.230 --> 00:08:39.630
For each point here is
generated by one disturbance,

00:08:39.630 --> 00:08:40.770
small u.

00:08:40.770 --> 00:08:44.760
So if you integrate out
this, the disturbance u,

00:08:44.760 --> 00:08:48.763
you get for each input
X, a distribution of Y's.

00:08:49.700 --> 00:08:53.870
Formally, this, after
integrating out the disturbance,

00:08:53.870 --> 00:08:55.480
you get a mathematical object

00:08:55.480 --> 00:08:57.890
that is called a Markov kernel.

00:08:57.890 --> 00:09:02.420
Sometimes you call it stochastic
matrix, or stochastic map.

00:09:02.420 --> 00:09:04.060
So the basic requirement here,

00:09:04.060 --> 00:09:09.060
is that for each X, you have
a distribution on the Y's.

00:09:09.230 --> 00:09:10.340
That's all.

00:09:10.340 --> 00:09:15.340
So, it means that Kappa of XY
is greater than or equal to 0,

00:09:15.420 --> 00:09:17.750
because that's the probability,

00:09:17.750 --> 00:09:20.520
and the sum over the Y's,

00:09:20.520 --> 00:09:23.260
or the integral over the Y's, should be 1.

00:09:23.260 --> 00:09:24.340
That's all.

00:09:24.340 --> 00:09:26.290
So that's the definition of a Markov,

00:09:26.290 --> 00:09:27.740
of a so-called Markov kernel,

00:09:28.750 --> 00:09:30.673
and that's the basic object,

00:09:32.100 --> 00:09:34.730
basic mathematical object that is used

00:09:34.730 --> 00:09:36.260
in order to model the mechanism.

00:09:36.260 --> 00:09:39.640
The mechanism in the
context of causal networks,

00:09:39.640 --> 00:09:44.640
is given in terms of a Markov
kernel, or stochastic map.

00:09:44.750 --> 00:09:47.800
As I said, this has been
used in many contexts,

00:09:47.800 --> 00:09:50.760
and with the same, you can do
the same construction here,

00:09:50.760 --> 00:09:52.083
in the context of,

00:09:53.030 --> 00:09:54.560
of quantum mechanics,

00:09:54.560 --> 00:09:55.520
and there you end up

00:09:55.520 --> 00:09:58.350
with the so-called
completely positive map,

00:09:58.350 --> 00:10:01.663
which is frequently used in
quantum information theory.

00:10:02.790 --> 00:10:04.740
So that's the building block.

00:10:04.740 --> 00:10:08.210
Now, the question is, how to
put together these mechanisms?

00:10:08.210 --> 00:10:13.210
The structure that describes
how to combine these mechanisms

00:10:13.480 --> 00:10:15.170
is a Directed-

00:10:15.170 --> 00:10:16.740
Acyclic-

00:10:16.740 --> 00:10:17.840
Graph,

00:10:17.840 --> 00:10:19.223
so, basically, it's-

00:10:20.490 --> 00:10:21.820
as shown here.

00:10:21.820 --> 00:10:25.543
So you have the nodes, these
are the variables, A, B, C, U.

00:10:27.558 --> 00:10:32.558
U is not the disturbance,
here, it's one variable.

00:10:34.890 --> 00:10:36.373
Basically,

00:10:37.290 --> 00:10:39.060
the semantics here,

00:10:39.060 --> 00:10:42.870
is whenever you have an arrow,
for example, from A to B,

00:10:42.870 --> 00:10:45.740
A is the direct cause of B.

00:10:45.740 --> 00:10:48.940
B is the effect, direct effect of A,

00:10:48.940 --> 00:10:50.560
and you also require

00:10:50.560 --> 00:10:53.553
that the cause always comes-

00:10:54.730 --> 00:10:57.320
before the effect, okay?

00:10:57.320 --> 00:11:00.560
That was the subject of
the previous presentation.

00:11:00.560 --> 00:11:02.210
So, the,

00:11:02.210 --> 00:11:06.650
the order has to be first the
cause, and then the effect.

00:11:06.650 --> 00:11:09.880
That excludes cycles like this,

00:11:09.880 --> 00:11:13.090
this is the reason why we have to assume

00:11:13.090 --> 00:11:14.540
that-

00:11:14.540 --> 00:11:16.380
the underlying structure is given

00:11:16.380 --> 00:11:19.053
in terms of a directed acyclic graph.

00:11:20.330 --> 00:11:24.700
So, some people actually
question this assumption, here,

00:11:24.700 --> 00:11:26.043
but it's crucial.

00:11:27.500 --> 00:11:28.333
So,

00:11:29.340 --> 00:11:31.500
we have, in the context of...

00:11:31.500 --> 00:11:33.210
Once given such a graph,

00:11:33.210 --> 00:11:35.980
you can talk about the
parents of a node V,

00:11:35.980 --> 00:11:37.223
denoted by pa,

00:11:38.390 --> 00:11:43.390
which are simply those
nodes that point to V,

00:11:43.660 --> 00:11:46.360
then the descendants of U,

00:11:46.360 --> 00:11:49.963
these are those nodes that can be reached,

00:11:51.013 --> 00:11:52.500
from U,

00:11:52.500 --> 00:11:55.460
the non-descendants, and the ancestors.

00:11:55.460 --> 00:11:58.860
So, basically, it's clear
from the naming, here,

00:11:58.860 --> 00:11:59.723
what it means.

00:12:01.210 --> 00:12:04.760
So, now, we have the graphical structure.

00:12:04.760 --> 00:12:08.290
In my first slide, I explained
what we mean by a mechanism.

00:12:08.290 --> 00:12:11.540
Now we have to put these
two structures together,

00:12:11.540 --> 00:12:12.373
so we-

00:12:14.307 --> 00:12:16.560
we start with a directed acyclic graph,

00:12:16.560 --> 00:12:18.770
that's the structure,

00:12:18.770 --> 00:12:19.603
and then we,

00:12:19.603 --> 00:12:22.740
we assume that, for each node,

00:12:22.740 --> 00:12:25.553
we have given such a Markov kernel,

00:12:27.110 --> 00:12:28.950
a mechanism, which, basically,

00:12:28.950 --> 00:12:31.700
is nothing than a stochastic map.

00:12:31.700 --> 00:12:34.750
So it takes the inputs,
for example, in X4, here,

00:12:34.750 --> 00:12:38.193
that node takes these as inputs,

00:12:39.050 --> 00:12:42.440
and generates a distribution over X4.

00:12:42.440 --> 00:12:46.150
So you have a mechanism in all nodes here.

00:12:46.150 --> 00:12:47.103
The only-

00:12:48.510 --> 00:12:51.730
node that does not get any input is X1,

00:12:51.730 --> 00:12:55.380
so that's simply a probability
distribution over X1,

00:12:55.380 --> 00:12:57.620
but all the others have mechanisms,

00:12:57.620 --> 00:12:58.473
sitting-

00:13:00.520 --> 00:13:01.353
in them.

00:13:03.130 --> 00:13:08.023
As I explained, whenever we
have a directed arrow here,

00:13:09.440 --> 00:13:13.480
we refer to v as being
the direct cause of w,

00:13:13.480 --> 00:13:17.290
and w being the direct cause of v

00:13:17.290 --> 00:13:19.360
and if I have such,

00:13:19.360 --> 00:13:20.363
this curly-

00:13:21.360 --> 00:13:25.683
arrow, that means that
there's a path from v to w.

00:13:26.740 --> 00:13:31.130
so in that case, I simply
talk about cause and effect,

00:13:31.130 --> 00:13:31.963
without-

00:13:34.950 --> 00:13:37.000
referring to,

00:13:37.000 --> 00:13:40.293
to it being directed, a direct cause.

00:13:41.470 --> 00:13:44.280
So, this is a simple example,

00:13:44.280 --> 00:13:47.370
taken from Judea Pearl's book,

00:13:47.370 --> 00:13:50.520
it's quite a famous book here,

00:13:50.520 --> 00:13:55.520
where the foundations of
cause networks are developed,

00:13:55.640 --> 00:13:58.880
and so I'm not going to,
into the details here,

00:13:58.880 --> 00:13:59.913
but with these,

00:14:02.648 --> 00:14:05.080
this kind of Bayesian network,

00:14:05.080 --> 00:14:09.500
you can actually describe
a causal structure,

00:14:09.500 --> 00:14:12.613
or causal interaction of variables.

00:14:14.490 --> 00:14:16.460
So this is a more complicate-

00:14:16.460 --> 00:14:18.773
these are more complicated networks,

00:14:19.614 --> 00:14:21.880
than the previous ones,

00:14:21.880 --> 00:14:24.400
which are more like toy examples,

00:14:24.400 --> 00:14:28.423
and these networks are taken
from, also a famous book,

00:14:32.330 --> 00:14:35.070
by leading experts of the field,

00:14:35.070 --> 00:14:38.770
by Lauritzen, and David,

00:14:38.770 --> 00:14:40.138
who were-

00:14:40.138 --> 00:14:40.971
and Spiegelhalter.

00:14:40.971 --> 00:14:42.793
Lauritzen's actually one of the-

00:14:44.150 --> 00:14:47.420
most famous people in
graphical models theory,

00:14:47.420 --> 00:14:50.420
so this kind of graphic representations

00:14:50.420 --> 00:14:51.743
of causal structures.

00:14:52.740 --> 00:14:55.160
Then I added, actually, this slide here.

00:14:55.160 --> 00:14:58.910
So I was, I had long conversation
with my daughter today,

00:14:58.910 --> 00:15:01.800
and tried to figure out
which movies to take here,

00:15:01.800 --> 00:15:05.690
which somehow tried to violate this idea

00:15:05.690 --> 00:15:08.410
of a directed acyclic graph.

00:15:08.410 --> 00:15:10.150
So you have time-travels,

00:15:10.150 --> 00:15:15.030
where you have loops between
the past and the future.

00:15:15.030 --> 00:15:17.640
So there are people, and
in these movies, actually,

00:15:17.640 --> 00:15:21.290
people try to justify, even, such loops,

00:15:21.290 --> 00:15:22.173
physically.

00:15:23.980 --> 00:15:25.720
And this-

00:15:25.720 --> 00:15:28.720
this movie here, Groundhog Day,

00:15:28.720 --> 00:15:31.643
was actually presented by
the Santa Fe Instituters,

00:15:33.010 --> 00:15:36.670
many years ago, and it was
commented by Murray Gell-Mann,

00:15:36.670 --> 00:15:39.880
who actually discovered the quarks,

00:15:39.880 --> 00:15:40.713
and-

00:15:42.198 --> 00:15:45.060
he was asked whether this
makes physical sense,

00:15:45.060 --> 00:15:45.893
to-

00:15:45.893 --> 00:15:49.610
the idea's to go to start again a new day,

00:15:49.610 --> 00:15:52.450
every day to start again,
and try to improve.

00:15:52.450 --> 00:15:56.040
So you go back, after, after
you spend the whole day,

00:15:56.040 --> 00:15:57.730
you go back to the beginning of the day,

00:15:57.730 --> 00:15:59.700
and try to improve your behavior,

00:15:59.700 --> 00:16:03.080
and that the end of the
day, of these iterations,

00:16:03.080 --> 00:16:05.550
you even become an
expert in piano-playing,

00:16:05.550 --> 00:16:08.420
even if you are not an
expert in the beginning.

00:16:08.420 --> 00:16:10.490
So you really have these loops,

00:16:10.490 --> 00:16:13.610
and which allow you to improve, here.

00:16:13.610 --> 00:16:15.813
And again, so it was actually-

00:16:17.550 --> 00:16:19.653
stated by Gell-Mann, that-

00:16:21.040 --> 00:16:25.040
this is, physically, a reasonable idea.

00:16:25.040 --> 00:16:27.510
And the same with the other movies.

00:16:27.510 --> 00:16:29.800
So, in this last movie here, Tenet,

00:16:29.800 --> 00:16:32.270
they even tried to,

00:16:32.270 --> 00:16:33.714
to build the whole story,

00:16:33.714 --> 00:16:37.000
based on the second law of thermodynamics,

00:16:37.000 --> 00:16:40.530
which was, as we have seen
in the last presentation,

00:16:40.530 --> 00:16:42.950
is a basic argument,

00:16:42.950 --> 00:16:44.470
on-

00:16:44.470 --> 00:16:46.660
explaining the direction,

00:16:46.660 --> 00:16:48.023
the direction of time.

00:16:49.410 --> 00:16:50.920
Okay,

00:16:50.920 --> 00:16:54.440
let me go to the second topic,

00:16:54.440 --> 00:16:58.830
so now once we have the
causal structure here,

00:16:58.830 --> 00:17:00.380
the causal network,

00:17:00.380 --> 00:17:03.860
we can define how the mechanisms,

00:17:03.860 --> 00:17:05.820
which are part of this network,

00:17:05.820 --> 00:17:08.550
did generate-

00:17:08.550 --> 00:17:09.790
the phenomena.

00:17:09.790 --> 00:17:12.890
So how they generate
actually a distribution.

00:17:12.890 --> 00:17:14.980
So, basically, it's a simple rule,

00:17:14.980 --> 00:17:18.350
you start, you have a
numbering of the nodes,

00:17:18.350 --> 00:17:21.333
which is compatible with that structure.

00:17:22.220 --> 00:17:24.017
So here, the numbering is,

00:17:24.017 --> 00:17:27.850
you start with U, then A, then B, then C,

00:17:27.850 --> 00:17:31.963
and then you, basically,
apply the mechanisms,

00:17:33.330 --> 00:17:34.910
according to this numbering.

00:17:34.910 --> 00:17:38.710
So you choose u according to
the probability distribution,

00:17:38.710 --> 00:17:39.930
phi of u.

00:17:39.930 --> 00:17:42.690
So it doesn't have any parents, here.

00:17:42.690 --> 00:17:45.090
Then you choose a,

00:17:45.090 --> 00:17:50.090
so this, according to the
distribution of A, given U,

00:17:50.360 --> 00:17:54.490
so this is a Markov kernel,
and then you iterate, okay?

00:17:54.490 --> 00:17:56.850
So these are the mechanisms.

00:17:56.850 --> 00:18:00.930
Note that I did not
use the letter P, here,

00:18:00.930 --> 00:18:04.020
really in order to refer,
make a distinction between,

00:18:04.020 --> 00:18:06.903
a mechanism, and the
probability distribution.

00:18:07.970 --> 00:18:10.690
So the right-hand side is basically,

00:18:10.690 --> 00:18:13.040
a combination of mechanisms,

00:18:13.040 --> 00:18:18.040
and it describes how the
probability distribution,

00:18:18.490 --> 00:18:19.323
that-

00:18:20.750 --> 00:18:21.583
of the-

00:18:24.220 --> 00:18:27.070
of joint events, on the full set.

00:18:27.070 --> 00:18:31.420
So the distribution, the
probability of u, a, b, c,

00:18:31.420 --> 00:18:34.660
is exactly given, in
terms of these mechanisms.

00:18:34.660 --> 00:18:35.523
So-

00:18:36.610 --> 00:18:37.443
I want to highlight here,

00:18:37.443 --> 00:18:39.610
that the left-hand side is, basically,

00:18:39.610 --> 00:18:41.730
describing the phenomenology,

00:18:41.730 --> 00:18:44.780
and the right-hand side is
describing the mechanisms.

00:18:44.780 --> 00:18:47.240
And this equation is giving you a rule,

00:18:47.240 --> 00:18:51.233
how to generate the phenomenon,
based on the mechanisms.

00:18:53.260 --> 00:18:55.047
Now we can ask the question:

00:18:55.047 --> 00:18:57.963
"Once we know the phenomena,

00:18:59.900 --> 00:19:01.480
the joint distribution,

00:19:01.480 --> 00:19:04.140
can we actually infer the mechanisms,

00:19:04.140 --> 00:19:06.267
based on these phenomena?"

00:19:09.613 --> 00:19:11.800
And the answer is,

00:19:11.800 --> 00:19:13.860
we can, we can try.

00:19:13.860 --> 00:19:17.080
The way people try it,
is in the following way.

00:19:17.080 --> 00:19:19.770
They take the distribution,

00:19:19.770 --> 00:19:21.050
the joint distribution,

00:19:21.050 --> 00:19:23.690
so this is the observed distribution,

00:19:23.690 --> 00:19:24.523
and then,

00:19:24.523 --> 00:19:27.760
you can actually test
condition-independent statements.

00:19:27.760 --> 00:19:30.960
So, if this distribution
is generated by mechanisms

00:19:30.960 --> 00:19:33.730
that are compatible with this graph,

00:19:33.730 --> 00:19:37.850
then it has to satisfy this
condition-independents,

00:19:37.850 --> 00:19:40.200
these two condition-independent
statements.

00:19:40.200 --> 00:19:44.030
So U is independence,
stochastically independent

00:19:44.030 --> 00:19:46.470
of B given A,

00:19:46.470 --> 00:19:49.410
and C is independent of A,

00:19:49.410 --> 00:19:51.610
given U and B.

00:19:51.610 --> 00:19:54.800
So, these are the two
condition-independent statements,

00:19:54.800 --> 00:19:57.810
that follow from this structure, here.

00:19:57.810 --> 00:20:01.500
So if you take the joint
distribution and do these tests,

00:20:01.500 --> 00:20:04.693
you will actually, you will
be able to verify this.

00:20:06.120 --> 00:20:11.120
The question is, do we recover
the underlying structure

00:20:11.130 --> 00:20:12.440
only by testing this,

00:20:12.440 --> 00:20:14.670
and the answer is no, we don't,

00:20:14.670 --> 00:20:17.920
because there are many more graphs,

00:20:17.920 --> 00:20:19.610
directed acyclic graphs,

00:20:19.610 --> 00:20:21.500
that satisfy the same set

00:20:21.500 --> 00:20:24.570
of condition-independent statements, okay?

00:20:24.570 --> 00:20:27.883
In this case, so that's this graph here,

00:20:28.820 --> 00:20:33.290
but you can also change,
modify this graph a bit,

00:20:33.290 --> 00:20:35.330
and it will give you the same set

00:20:35.330 --> 00:20:37.440
of conditions-independent statements.

00:20:37.440 --> 00:20:40.523
And this is actually
referred to as Markov-

00:20:42.520 --> 00:20:43.353
equivalence.

00:20:43.353 --> 00:20:46.250
So all three graphs would
be Markov equivalent,

00:20:46.250 --> 00:20:47.630
in the sense that they will give you

00:20:47.630 --> 00:20:50.060
the same condition-independent statements.

00:20:50.060 --> 00:20:52.910
So, once you have generated,
with the mechanisms,

00:20:52.910 --> 00:20:55.483
the joint distribution, so the phenomenon,

00:20:56.840 --> 00:21:01.290
once you have reached the
phenomenological level,

00:21:01.290 --> 00:21:04.000
you cannot go back to
the to the mechanisms,

00:21:04.000 --> 00:21:05.780
simply by observing and testing

00:21:05.780 --> 00:21:08.290
the condition-independent statements.

00:21:08.290 --> 00:21:10.290
So, there is a-

00:21:11.320 --> 00:21:12.193
a whole-

00:21:13.220 --> 00:21:17.073
the theory is well-developed,
that describes, actually,

00:21:18.100 --> 00:21:22.020
the equivalence, Markov
equivalence classes of graphs.

00:21:22.020 --> 00:21:23.870
So it's a well-known theory.

00:21:23.870 --> 00:21:26.340
I'm going to skip this,

00:21:26.340 --> 00:21:30.233
and continue with section number three.

00:21:31.170 --> 00:21:33.910
So the intention, of this,

00:21:33.910 --> 00:21:34.990
the Markov-

00:21:34.990 --> 00:21:38.040
my presentation of Markov equivalence

00:21:38.040 --> 00:21:42.870
is to show you that just observing
the system is not enough.

00:21:42.870 --> 00:21:44.090
You can observe,

00:21:44.090 --> 00:21:46.161
but you will not be able to recover

00:21:46.161 --> 00:21:49.960
the full underlying structure,

00:21:49.960 --> 00:21:51.950
simply by observation.

00:21:51.950 --> 00:21:54.560
So this is why Pearl actually introduces

00:21:54.560 --> 00:21:55.900
the notion of intervention.

00:21:55.900 --> 00:21:58.910
So you have to be able to
intervene into the system.

00:21:58.910 --> 00:22:01.420
And this is a second kind of experiment,

00:22:01.420 --> 00:22:03.750
so experimental operation, if you wish.

00:22:03.750 --> 00:22:06.630
One experimental operation is observation,

00:22:06.630 --> 00:22:09.345
and the second one we are
going to talk about now,

00:22:09.345 --> 00:22:11.850
is intervention.

00:22:11.850 --> 00:22:13.700
And I'm going to define intervention,

00:22:13.700 --> 00:22:15.813
I have to refer to the previous-

00:22:17.690 --> 00:22:18.680
presentation.

00:22:18.680 --> 00:22:21.623
Intervention was also
mentioned several times,

00:22:23.650 --> 00:22:27.050
especially when stating that the future

00:22:27.050 --> 00:22:30.240
can be influenced through
intervention, but not the past.

00:22:30.240 --> 00:22:33.010
So that was that, that
can actually be verified,

00:22:33.010 --> 00:22:35.363
within this setting, here.

00:22:37.060 --> 00:22:40.340
So, let me define intervention.

00:22:40.340 --> 00:22:41.550
Let's say...

00:22:42.650 --> 00:22:44.235
Let's assume that this is the,

00:22:44.235 --> 00:22:45.973
the causal-

00:22:47.790 --> 00:22:48.990
network.

00:22:48.990 --> 00:22:51.120
So we have the directed acyclic graph,

00:22:51.120 --> 00:22:54.470
and we have the mechanisms,
alpha, beta, gamma.

00:22:54.470 --> 00:22:56.523
We want to intervene in A,

00:22:57.860 --> 00:22:59.523
and then observe B.

00:23:00.620 --> 00:23:02.083
So what does this mean?

00:23:06.230 --> 00:23:09.150
So, intervention, in
A, means the following.

00:23:09.150 --> 00:23:13.060
If we, if we consider the
full joint distribution,

00:23:13.060 --> 00:23:16.110
according to the original
mechanisms, alpha beta and gamma,

00:23:16.110 --> 00:23:18.970
it will be given,
according to this formula.

00:23:18.970 --> 00:23:23.043
That's the formula that
I have just discussed.

00:23:24.230 --> 00:23:26.940
So now,

00:23:26.940 --> 00:23:28.120
you could observe

00:23:28.120 --> 00:23:32.600
the conditional probability of B, given A,

00:23:32.600 --> 00:23:35.450
that using standard probability theory,

00:23:35.450 --> 00:23:37.750
but intervention means
something different.

00:23:37.750 --> 00:23:41.890
Intervention means changing the mechanism.

00:23:41.890 --> 00:23:44.270
So, in this product-structure here,

00:23:44.270 --> 00:23:48.130
we have, in A, we have
the mechanism, alpha.

00:23:48.130 --> 00:23:50.090
Alpha takes input from U,

00:23:50.090 --> 00:23:52.670
and generates a distribution-

00:23:52.670 --> 00:23:55.000
of small a's,

00:23:55.000 --> 00:23:56.760
according to alpha. Okay?

00:23:56.760 --> 00:23:59.433
That's the Markov kernel, sitting in A.

00:24:00.360 --> 00:24:02.690
Now, if we intervene in A,

00:24:02.690 --> 00:24:06.840
let's say we want to set the state of A,

00:24:06.840 --> 00:24:08.023
to a hat.

00:24:09.660 --> 00:24:13.250
Then, that means that we decouple...

00:24:13.250 --> 00:24:15.810
Basically we change the mechanism of A,

00:24:15.810 --> 00:24:17.780
by replacing it,

00:24:17.780 --> 00:24:18.973
by alpha hat,

00:24:20.020 --> 00:24:24.220
and alpha hat is simply
very special Markov kernel,

00:24:24.220 --> 00:24:27.363
which is 1, it gives the distribution 1.

00:24:28.500 --> 00:24:30.440
So the probability of a is one,

00:24:30.440 --> 00:24:34.330
if a equals a hat, and zero, otherwise.

00:24:34.330 --> 00:24:37.890
So this is nothing but saying that-

00:24:37.890 --> 00:24:39.580
we set the state of A,

00:24:39.580 --> 00:24:41.830
to a hat, that's it.

00:24:41.830 --> 00:24:46.830
And in order to stay with my
previous formal description,

00:24:48.260 --> 00:24:50.010
I need to define a Markov kernel,

00:24:50.010 --> 00:24:52.150
and that's the way I do it, here.

00:24:52.150 --> 00:24:55.230
Formally, it simply means
changing the mechanism

00:24:55.230 --> 00:24:57.800
to a constant value,

00:24:57.800 --> 00:24:58.980
a hat.

00:24:58.980 --> 00:25:01.890
And now, instead of this
product structure here,

00:25:01.890 --> 00:25:04.830
we have a new product structure,

00:25:04.830 --> 00:25:06.000
so that's the-

00:25:06.000 --> 00:25:08.413
we get a new causal-

00:25:09.760 --> 00:25:11.170
network,

00:25:11.170 --> 00:25:14.910
but now the mechanism in
A is changed to a hat,

00:25:14.910 --> 00:25:17.460
ah, alpha hat, from alpha to alpha hat.

00:25:17.460 --> 00:25:20.190
So phi remains the same,
beta remains the same,

00:25:20.190 --> 00:25:25.190
gamma remains the same, and
alpha is replaced by alpha hat.

00:25:26.000 --> 00:25:26.850
And that's it.

00:25:26.850 --> 00:25:29.443
That's the post-interventional
distribution.

00:25:30.280 --> 00:25:31.353
Now, let's-

00:25:33.260 --> 00:25:34.210
consider,

00:25:34.210 --> 00:25:35.750
so what I have shown to you here,

00:25:35.750 --> 00:25:39.790
is the post-interventional
joint distribution,

00:25:39.790 --> 00:25:42.240
after imposing a hat.

00:25:42.240 --> 00:25:46.200
Now I want to marginalize out U, B and C,

00:25:46.200 --> 00:25:50.979
just to know the post-intervention
distribution over B,

00:25:50.979 --> 00:25:52.553
imposing A.

00:25:53.450 --> 00:25:55.370
So that means,

00:25:55.370 --> 00:25:57.730
so that's the thing we want to compute,

00:25:57.730 --> 00:26:02.073
so, what do we see in
B if we impose a hat?

00:26:03.020 --> 00:26:07.100
So that's basically marginalizing out

00:26:07.100 --> 00:26:09.273
all the others, U and C.

00:26:11.350 --> 00:26:15.010
So we take this
post-intervention distribution,

00:26:15.010 --> 00:26:17.490
that I have derived previously,

00:26:17.490 --> 00:26:19.190
and marginalize out,

00:26:19.190 --> 00:26:21.740
and that has the product structure.

00:26:21.740 --> 00:26:24.060
Then we can go through the calculation,

00:26:24.060 --> 00:26:27.193
and you get p of b as the result,

00:26:28.522 --> 00:26:30.430
of the intervention.

00:26:30.430 --> 00:26:33.260
So that means that the-

00:26:33.260 --> 00:26:35.670
effect of-

00:26:35.670 --> 00:26:37.330
intervening in A,

00:26:37.330 --> 00:26:38.230
is simply...

00:26:38.230 --> 00:26:41.960
so if I intervene in A and
set the state to a hat,

00:26:41.960 --> 00:26:46.960
I will observe B with the
original probability, p of b.

00:26:47.630 --> 00:26:51.033
The important thing to
note, here, is that b,

00:26:52.080 --> 00:26:56.960
that probability distribution
is not dependent on a hat.

00:26:56.960 --> 00:26:58.660
So it's different from it.

00:26:58.660 --> 00:27:00.800
This is really something
that you don't get,

00:27:00.800 --> 00:27:02.380
with-

00:27:02.380 --> 00:27:04.810
with classical conditioning.

00:27:04.810 --> 00:27:06.900
So, with classical conditioning,

00:27:06.900 --> 00:27:09.590
the condition probability of B,

00:27:09.590 --> 00:27:12.530
given A, as shown here,

00:27:12.530 --> 00:27:15.223
will be actually dependent on A.

00:27:16.170 --> 00:27:19.010
But when you, intuitively
you will, you would not,

00:27:19.010 --> 00:27:20.470
because there's no arrow here,

00:27:20.470 --> 00:27:24.040
you would not expect any effect
in B, if you intervene in A,

00:27:24.040 --> 00:27:27.030
because there is no path from A to B.

00:27:27.030 --> 00:27:29.380
And this is exactly what you get here.

00:27:29.380 --> 00:27:30.960
So as the result of intervention,

00:27:30.960 --> 00:27:33.150
you get simply the distribution of B,

00:27:33.150 --> 00:27:36.193
with no dependence on a hat.

00:27:37.060 --> 00:27:40.470
So, this reflects our intuition
that there is no path,

00:27:40.470 --> 00:27:42.170
from A to B, okay?

00:27:42.170 --> 00:27:44.430
- [Priya] Hold on, we have,
I just had a quick question.

00:27:44.430 --> 00:27:48.360
So we are still talking about
deterministic systems, right?

00:27:48.360 --> 00:27:49.670
So,

00:27:49.670 --> 00:27:52.600
that there isn't, when we
say there's no path between,

00:27:52.600 --> 00:27:53.840
from A to B,

00:27:53.840 --> 00:27:58.330
do you mean that there is a
very suppressed probability

00:27:58.330 --> 00:28:00.330
for a path from A to B,

00:28:00.330 --> 00:28:02.310
or there really is no path,

00:28:02.310 --> 00:28:03.670
from A to B?
- [Nihat] There is no,

00:28:03.670 --> 00:28:05.750
no path, from A to B.

00:28:05.750 --> 00:28:08.030
So that's the assumption, here.

00:28:08.030 --> 00:28:10.850
So the underlying, the structure of it,

00:28:10.850 --> 00:28:14.040
is a directed acyclic graph,

00:28:14.040 --> 00:28:17.320
and some of the edges
are simply not there.

00:28:17.320 --> 00:28:18.930
So that means there's no causal-

00:28:18.930 --> 00:28:21.210
if no possibility...

00:28:21.210 --> 00:28:24.110
It's like the future-

00:28:24.110 --> 00:28:26.570
cause, influencing the past.

00:28:26.570 --> 00:28:27.460
- [Priya] Right.

00:28:27.460 --> 00:28:28.550
- [Nihat] Intuitively, you would say

00:28:28.550 --> 00:28:30.150
there is no possibility.

00:28:30.150 --> 00:28:32.250
Even no low-probability.

00:28:32.250 --> 00:28:33.500
Okay?

00:28:33.500 --> 00:28:34.483
So simply...
- And that is independent

00:28:34.483 --> 00:28:37.653
of whether the system
is classical or quantum?

00:28:38.970 --> 00:28:40.720
Right, so is it...
- [Nihat] So the quantum

00:28:40.720 --> 00:28:43.150
version of this is not,

00:28:43.150 --> 00:28:44.470
is not well-developed.

00:28:44.470 --> 00:28:47.720
So I'm, I was referring to quantum setting

00:28:47.720 --> 00:28:49.490
in the context of a mechanism.

00:28:49.490 --> 00:28:52.610
So, each of these factors here,

00:28:52.610 --> 00:28:54.940
are Markov kernels,

00:28:54.940 --> 00:28:56.640
and in the quantum setting,

00:28:56.640 --> 00:28:59.090
this would be completely positive maps,

00:28:59.090 --> 00:29:03.243
but the theory of causal networks
is not well developed in,

00:29:04.559 --> 00:29:05.920
in the quantum setting.

00:29:05.920 --> 00:29:08.500
But the notion of a mechanism is,

00:29:08.500 --> 00:29:10.420
has an analog in the quantum setting.

00:29:10.420 --> 00:29:12.170
- [Priya] Okay, thank you.

00:29:12.170 --> 00:29:14.320
- [Nihat] You are welcome.

00:29:14.320 --> 00:29:15.343
So-

00:29:17.100 --> 00:29:19.457
yeah, so we have the
post-intervention distribution here,

00:29:19.457 --> 00:29:23.470
and it really is different
from the usual conditioning,

00:29:23.470 --> 00:29:25.400
p of b, given-

00:29:25.400 --> 00:29:27.523
observing a hat.

00:29:28.560 --> 00:29:32.253
But now let's do the same
thing, now intervening in U,

00:29:33.220 --> 00:29:34.770
and observing C.

00:29:34.770 --> 00:29:37.203
So we can do the same calculation here,

00:29:38.070 --> 00:29:39.770
a similar calculation.

00:29:39.770 --> 00:29:42.913
So P of C, imposing u hat,

00:29:44.780 --> 00:29:46.200
and if you go through it,

00:29:46.200 --> 00:29:48.530
this time, it turns out,

00:29:48.530 --> 00:29:53.530
that it's the same
post-interventional distribution

00:29:54.090 --> 00:29:57.410
that you get if you condition

00:29:57.410 --> 00:30:01.020
according to the classical
conditional distribution.

00:30:01.020 --> 00:30:03.070
So that's the classical version of it

00:30:03.070 --> 00:30:05.760
would be p of c comma u hat,

00:30:05.760 --> 00:30:08.000
divided by p of u hat.

00:30:08.000 --> 00:30:09.850
That's the classical version of it.

00:30:09.850 --> 00:30:13.200
And we have seen here,
that it's not the same,

00:30:13.200 --> 00:30:15.130
but in this case, it is the same.

00:30:15.130 --> 00:30:17.023
So the do operator,

00:30:18.050 --> 00:30:20.820
the intervention operator,

00:30:20.820 --> 00:30:23.400
is exactly the same in this example,

00:30:23.400 --> 00:30:26.670
as the classical conditioning operator.

00:30:26.670 --> 00:30:27.503
Okay?

00:30:28.521 --> 00:30:30.440
And that has a reason, actually.

00:30:30.440 --> 00:30:33.493
So you can sometimes,
as we see, sometimes,

00:30:34.580 --> 00:30:36.010
the intervention

00:30:36.010 --> 00:30:38.670
gives you the
post-interventional distribution,

00:30:38.670 --> 00:30:40.540
is the same as the...

00:30:42.210 --> 00:30:43.480
Interventional conditioning

00:30:43.480 --> 00:30:45.840
is the same as classical conditioning,

00:30:45.840 --> 00:30:47.453
and sometimes it's not.

00:30:48.290 --> 00:30:50.433
And let me just summarize, here.

00:30:51.380 --> 00:30:52.430
So how we,

00:30:52.430 --> 00:30:54.670
what we just did,

00:30:54.670 --> 00:30:56.670
or maybe I can just skip this,

00:30:56.670 --> 00:30:57.930
so there is a general-

00:30:57.930 --> 00:31:01.200
general formula for-

00:31:01.200 --> 00:31:03.990
for computing the
post-intervention distribution,

00:31:03.990 --> 00:31:05.370
but I'll skip this.

00:31:05.370 --> 00:31:07.640
So here's the answer,

00:31:07.640 --> 00:31:10.130
when the intervention,

00:31:10.130 --> 00:31:11.620
interventional conditioning

00:31:11.620 --> 00:31:14.823
gives you the same as the
observational conditioning.

00:31:15.780 --> 00:31:19.530
So the do means, we intervene in A,

00:31:19.530 --> 00:31:20.943
and observe B,

00:31:21.830 --> 00:31:23.853
and that's the distribution over-

00:31:24.810 --> 00:31:25.830
over-

00:31:25.830 --> 00:31:26.663
B,

00:31:27.540 --> 00:31:30.170
imposing in A,

00:31:30.170 --> 00:31:32.470
and that's the conditional distribution.

00:31:32.470 --> 00:31:35.733
And they are the same, if, and only if,

00:31:38.800 --> 00:31:39.670
there is-

00:31:39.670 --> 00:31:40.503
B is-

00:31:43.420 --> 00:31:46.190
so they are the same, if
B is not a cause of A,

00:31:47.340 --> 00:31:49.887
and there is no common cause of A and B,

00:31:49.887 --> 00:31:52.360
and you can read it out structurally.

00:31:52.360 --> 00:31:54.783
So for example, if we look at A and B,

00:31:56.030 --> 00:31:58.400
so there- B is not the cause of A,

00:31:58.400 --> 00:32:00.900
because there is no path from B to A,

00:32:00.900 --> 00:32:02.590
so that's satisfied,

00:32:02.590 --> 00:32:04.560
and there's no common cause of A and B.

00:32:04.560 --> 00:32:05.713
So there is no-

00:32:07.460 --> 00:32:10.230
node pointing to A and B.

00:32:10.230 --> 00:32:13.030
So, if we revert this direction,

00:32:13.030 --> 00:32:15.690
then there would be a common cause here.

00:32:15.690 --> 00:32:18.990
So if this is satisfied, so
this condition is satisfied,

00:32:18.990 --> 00:32:21.890
then the interventional
conditioning is the same

00:32:21.890 --> 00:32:24.516
as the observation conditioning.

00:32:24.516 --> 00:32:28.133
But, if we look at C and B,

00:32:29.750 --> 00:32:31.560
there is a common cause of-

00:32:31.560 --> 00:32:33.540
I'm sorry, C,

00:32:33.540 --> 00:32:34.373
yeah.

00:32:34.373 --> 00:32:36.000
B and C, yeah, B and C.

00:32:36.000 --> 00:32:39.270
So C is not the cause of B,

00:32:39.270 --> 00:32:42.510
so the first requirement is met,

00:32:42.510 --> 00:32:44.530
but there is a common cause of B and C.

00:32:44.530 --> 00:32:45.520
It's this one.

00:32:45.520 --> 00:32:49.960
So we have U, which is
with a directed path,

00:32:49.960 --> 00:32:50.920
from U to B,

00:32:50.920 --> 00:32:53.040
and the directed path from U to C.

00:32:53.040 --> 00:32:55.150
So there's a common cause of B and C,

00:32:55.150 --> 00:32:56.460
and in that case,

00:32:56.460 --> 00:32:59.360
we cannot expect the intervention

00:32:59.360 --> 00:33:01.760
to be the same as observation.

00:33:01.760 --> 00:33:06.020
Okay? And the same with this case,

00:33:06.020 --> 00:33:08.330
the causal effect of A on C,

00:33:08.330 --> 00:33:11.130
we have a common cause on A and C,

00:33:11.130 --> 00:33:13.150
So again, we don't have equality.

00:33:13.150 --> 00:33:15.880
So this characterizes
exactly the situations

00:33:15.880 --> 00:33:19.200
where intervention
differs from observation.

00:33:19.200 --> 00:33:21.670
But intervention gives us more.

00:33:21.670 --> 00:33:23.023
And now comes-

00:33:25.610 --> 00:33:28.313
now comes a really important thing that-

00:33:30.950 --> 00:33:34.713
notion, the notion of
identifiability of causal effects.

00:33:36.440 --> 00:33:37.333
So,

00:33:38.684 --> 00:33:41.672
let me motivate this a little bit.

00:33:41.672 --> 00:33:46.330
We know intervention gives
us more, some information,

00:33:46.330 --> 00:33:49.300
sometimes more information
than just observing the system.

00:33:49.300 --> 00:33:51.103
This is what I tried to-

00:33:53.270 --> 00:33:55.270
to demonstrate here.

00:33:55.270 --> 00:33:58.330
But often, I mean, if we
know all the mechanisms,

00:33:58.330 --> 00:34:00.830
I have shown you the formula
for the intervention,

00:34:00.830 --> 00:34:04.570
you could simply compute the
post-intervention distribution,

00:34:04.570 --> 00:34:07.340
but that's, that doesn't help as much,

00:34:07.340 --> 00:34:09.020
because we do the intervention

00:34:09.020 --> 00:34:11.500
in order to get the mechanisms,

00:34:11.500 --> 00:34:13.790
so that's the chicken/egg problem, okay?

00:34:13.790 --> 00:34:15.580
So we don't know all the mechanisms,

00:34:15.580 --> 00:34:18.000
so that we can actually-

00:34:18.000 --> 00:34:21.000
compute the post-intervention
distributions.

00:34:21.000 --> 00:34:24.010
So, on the other hand, in experiments,

00:34:24.010 --> 00:34:26.423
so in experimental intervention setting,

00:34:27.560 --> 00:34:30.330
we take a system, a natural system,

00:34:30.330 --> 00:34:34.130
and we do intervene into
the system, experimentally.

00:34:34.130 --> 00:34:38.153
So we don't do the computation,
so what will happen,

00:34:39.510 --> 00:34:40.960
but we simply test it.

00:34:40.960 --> 00:34:44.060
So we do the intervention,
and observe the system,

00:34:44.060 --> 00:34:46.020
and see if there's any effect.

00:34:46.020 --> 00:34:48.053
So that's the experimental intervention.

00:34:49.260 --> 00:34:51.690
But this, of course, we cannot do all...

00:34:51.690 --> 00:34:53.910
I mean, sometimes there
are ethical problems,

00:34:53.910 --> 00:34:56.500
you cannot intervene into
the brain of a person,

00:34:56.500 --> 00:34:58.270
that's simply not possible, okay.

00:34:58.270 --> 00:35:00.210
So this is like a...

00:35:00.210 --> 00:35:04.860
You know that you can get more
information out of the system

00:35:04.860 --> 00:35:06.540
if you intervened experimentally,

00:35:06.540 --> 00:35:09.020
but sometimes it's simply not possible.

00:35:09.020 --> 00:35:12.040
So the question now, and
the deep question, is,

00:35:12.040 --> 00:35:17.040
can we predict the
outcome of intervention,

00:35:17.510 --> 00:35:20.700
even without actually
intervening into the system,

00:35:20.700 --> 00:35:22.483
simply by observing it?

00:35:24.014 --> 00:35:26.070
And that's the question

00:35:26.070 --> 00:35:28.603
of identifiability of causal effects.

00:35:29.930 --> 00:35:32.900
The answer is sometimes we can,

00:35:32.900 --> 00:35:35.130
and here's an example,

00:35:35.130 --> 00:35:37.400
I have two examples.

00:35:37.400 --> 00:35:39.623
So one is actually-

00:35:41.370 --> 00:35:43.387
I refer to it as the backdoor example,

00:35:43.387 --> 00:35:45.500
and the next one will be
the front-door example.

00:35:45.500 --> 00:35:47.250
These are typical examples,

00:35:47.250 --> 00:35:50.610
which you can study in Pearl's book.

00:35:50.610 --> 00:35:54.410
So if you intervene in B, and observe C,

00:35:54.410 --> 00:35:57.373
so we do the same calculation
that we did before.

00:35:58.872 --> 00:36:00.310
The marginalization steps,

00:36:00.310 --> 00:36:01.990
then you have the joint distribution,

00:36:01.990 --> 00:36:03.200
and the joint distribution

00:36:03.200 --> 00:36:05.820
you can replace by the mechanisms,

00:36:05.820 --> 00:36:07.697
and then do the calculation here,

00:36:07.697 --> 00:36:09.847
and then you end up
with this formula here.

00:36:10.950 --> 00:36:13.270
And the nice thing about
it, is the following:

00:36:13.270 --> 00:36:16.093
on the left-hand side,
you have the do operation,

00:36:17.106 --> 00:36:21.970
so, which basically says
if you intervene in B,

00:36:21.970 --> 00:36:25.560
you will, if you did this, if
you do this experimentally,

00:36:25.560 --> 00:36:28.713
you will observe this distribution on c.

00:36:29.870 --> 00:36:32.540
But if you don't do it experimentally,

00:36:32.540 --> 00:36:34.830
you can simply go
through this calculation,

00:36:34.830 --> 00:36:36.470
and read out this equa...

00:36:36.470 --> 00:36:38.070
this-

00:36:38.070 --> 00:36:39.420
expression here.

00:36:39.420 --> 00:36:44.150
So this expression can
be completely computed,

00:36:44.150 --> 00:36:48.510
based on the joint
distribution of A, B and C.

00:36:48.510 --> 00:36:51.930
So this is simply p of a comma b comma c,

00:36:51.930 --> 00:36:55.110
divided by p of a comma b,

00:36:55.110 --> 00:36:58.770
and this is p of a, so
that's all computable,

00:36:58.770 --> 00:37:03.653
by simply observing the joint
distribution, A, B and C.

00:37:04.500 --> 00:37:05.870
And that's,

00:37:05.870 --> 00:37:08.460
somewhat confusing, but-

00:37:08.460 --> 00:37:12.910
yeah, so it basically
suggests that you can replace

00:37:12.910 --> 00:37:14.916
the actual intervention here,

00:37:14.916 --> 00:37:16.680
by-

00:37:16.680 --> 00:37:17.710
observation,

00:37:17.710 --> 00:37:19.460
by the information that you get,

00:37:19.460 --> 00:37:23.220
in terms of observing the system,

00:37:23.220 --> 00:37:26.870
but you have to change,
somehow, the formula.

00:37:26.870 --> 00:37:31.870
So it's not just p of c given
b in the classical setting,

00:37:33.600 --> 00:37:36.140
so that would, if you condition a here,

00:37:36.140 --> 00:37:38.230
if you write p of a,

00:37:38.230 --> 00:37:39.500
given-

00:37:39.500 --> 00:37:40.550
b,

00:37:40.550 --> 00:37:41.383
here,

00:37:41.383 --> 00:37:42.380
instead of p of a,

00:37:42.380 --> 00:37:46.180
then you will end up with p of c,

00:37:46.180 --> 00:37:48.170
given b, in the classical way.

00:37:48.170 --> 00:37:50.390
But this formula is, so to say,

00:37:50.390 --> 00:37:52.870
different from the classical formula,

00:37:52.870 --> 00:37:54.680
but it, this equation tells you

00:37:54.680 --> 00:37:56.380
that you can actually predict

00:37:57.805 --> 00:38:00.070
the post-interventional distribution,

00:38:00.070 --> 00:38:02.240
based on observations.

00:38:02.240 --> 00:38:04.820
So, in this setting, and
the terminology of Pearl,

00:38:04.820 --> 00:38:08.400
we can say that the causal effect

00:38:08.400 --> 00:38:10.100
of b on c,

00:38:10.100 --> 00:38:15.030
is identifiable by the joint
distribution, A, B, and C.

00:38:16.473 --> 00:38:17.306
Okay?

00:38:17.306 --> 00:38:20.360
So we don't really
intervene to the system,

00:38:20.360 --> 00:38:22.250
we simply observe,

00:38:22.250 --> 00:38:25.800
and then we can compute
what what would happen,

00:38:25.800 --> 00:38:28.230
if we intervened into the system.

00:38:28.230 --> 00:38:29.823
So that's the philosophical-

00:38:34.558 --> 00:38:35.725
thought, here.

00:38:38.030 --> 00:38:38.863
So,

00:38:39.840 --> 00:38:42.370
for example, we can
use it in this setting,

00:38:42.370 --> 00:38:44.960
so I tried to draw a large network here,

00:38:44.960 --> 00:38:46.350
so it's of course not huge,

00:38:46.350 --> 00:38:47.703
but it's-

00:38:50.640 --> 00:38:52.780
enough to demonstrate the point, here.

00:38:52.780 --> 00:38:55.880
So, if you have such a network,

00:38:55.880 --> 00:39:00.880
and you want to intervene
in V, and observe w,

00:39:01.040 --> 00:39:05.163
okay, so what is the
causal effect of V on w?

00:39:06.110 --> 00:39:08.890
So you could, of course, if
you knew all the mechanisms,

00:39:08.890 --> 00:39:12.400
you could compute this,
as I have demonstrated,

00:39:12.400 --> 00:39:14.580
but this we don't have.

00:39:14.580 --> 00:39:16.530
So the question is...

00:39:16.530 --> 00:39:19.890
And if you just observe the
joint distribution of V and w,

00:39:19.890 --> 00:39:22.560
you can compute the
conditional distribution of V,

00:39:22.560 --> 00:39:24.660
of w given V.

00:39:24.660 --> 00:39:29.080
But the, the backdoor criterion
tells us, so this formula,

00:39:29.080 --> 00:39:31.610
tells us that we can actually compute

00:39:31.610 --> 00:39:33.780
what would happen,

00:39:33.780 --> 00:39:34.613
in w,

00:39:34.613 --> 00:39:36.600
if we intervened in V,

00:39:36.600 --> 00:39:39.910
by just observing V, w,

00:39:39.910 --> 00:39:42.070
and, in addition to that,

00:39:42.070 --> 00:39:43.633
the parents of V.

00:39:44.490 --> 00:39:45.360
So you see it,

00:39:45.360 --> 00:39:46.723
so the inter-

00:39:48.270 --> 00:39:49.180
the causal effect

00:39:49.180 --> 00:39:53.260
of the post-intervention
distribution on w,

00:39:53.260 --> 00:39:55.253
imposing xv,

00:39:56.420 --> 00:39:57.720
on the left-hand side,

00:39:57.720 --> 00:39:59.940
so that's an interventional concept,

00:39:59.940 --> 00:40:02.750
can be written as something
which is computable,

00:40:02.750 --> 00:40:05.090
based on observations only.

00:40:05.090 --> 00:40:10.010
So, by observing v, w
and the parents of v,

00:40:10.010 --> 00:40:12.670
no matter what the
surrounding is of the system,

00:40:12.670 --> 00:40:15.030
and how huge it is, it doesn't matter.

00:40:15.030 --> 00:40:17.490
You only need the joint distribution

00:40:17.490 --> 00:40:20.030
of v, w, and the parents,

00:40:20.030 --> 00:40:23.100
and then you will be able
to predict the outcome

00:40:23.100 --> 00:40:25.370
of intervention, without intervening.

00:40:25.370 --> 00:40:28.720
So, in other words, if you take the brain,

00:40:28.720 --> 00:40:33.083
and you can, you could, if
you knew the parents of each,

00:40:33.930 --> 00:40:35.880
of a particular neuron,

00:40:35.880 --> 00:40:40.187
you could actually predict
the effect of that neuron

00:40:40.187 --> 00:40:42.800
on some other region in the brain,

00:40:42.800 --> 00:40:45.700
simply based on this joint distribution.

00:40:45.700 --> 00:40:46.893
So there's a question.

