01:14:22.300 --> 01:14:23.913
- It, the thing-

01:14:26.160 --> 01:14:27.600
the reason for that,

01:14:27.600 --> 01:14:30.330
is that you have conditioned
independent statements.

01:14:30.330 --> 01:14:31.163
So the-

01:14:36.560 --> 01:14:40.020
basically in any,

01:14:40.020 --> 01:14:42.030
directed acyclic graph,

01:14:42.030 --> 01:14:43.643
so in any Bayesian network,

01:14:46.573 --> 01:14:51.080
the node is independent
of its non-descendants,

01:14:51.080 --> 01:14:54.030
in particular, independent
of its ancestors,

01:14:54.030 --> 01:14:58.110
given its direct causes,

01:14:58.110 --> 01:14:59.353
which are the parents.

01:15:00.620 --> 01:15:02.290
So you have always, for each node,

01:15:02.290 --> 01:15:05.410
each node is independent
of its non-descendants,

01:15:05.410 --> 01:15:07.890
given its direct causes.

01:15:07.890 --> 01:15:08.723
And-

01:15:10.147 --> 01:15:12.860
that's their so-called local-

01:15:12.860 --> 01:15:15.070
Markov property,

01:15:15.070 --> 01:15:18.230
which basically means,
if you know your parents,

01:15:18.230 --> 01:15:19.300
the state of your parents,

01:15:19.300 --> 01:15:22.060
you don't need to know more.

01:15:22.060 --> 01:15:25.020
Any additional information
about your ancestors,

01:15:25.020 --> 01:15:26.680
or even non-descendants,

01:15:26.680 --> 01:15:29.793
will not help you to to predict any-

01:15:32.240 --> 01:15:34.160
will not improve your predictions.

01:15:34.160 --> 01:15:35.100
- Right. So you're just,

01:15:35.100 --> 01:15:37.360
it's sufficient to go just one layer deep,

01:15:37.360 --> 01:15:39.060
in (indistinct).
- Exactly.

01:15:39.060 --> 01:15:40.023
