How does predictability of
future states of the system,

01:16:31.700 --> 01:16:34.570
assuming you can figure out
the mechanism, and so on.

01:16:34.570 --> 01:16:37.550
Right? So is that connected to...

01:16:39.320 --> 01:16:40.153
- Not really.

01:16:40.153 --> 01:16:41.030
I mean, there is...

01:16:41.030 --> 01:16:44.790
So the thing is, that the causal network,

01:16:44.790 --> 01:16:49.173
is really coupled with
conditional independence.

01:16:50.400 --> 01:16:52.613
So, the structure is,

01:16:53.691 --> 01:16:55.450
so there's a one-to-one correspondence

01:16:55.450 --> 01:16:57.330
between the structure, the graph,

01:16:57.330 --> 01:17:00.004
and condition-independent statements.

01:17:00.004 --> 01:17:03.770
And, in the context of a
dynamical system, for example,

01:17:03.770 --> 01:17:06.260
you can, if you represent it in this way,

01:17:06.260 --> 01:17:07.093
you can say

01:17:07.093 --> 01:17:10.490
the future is conditionally
independent of the past,

01:17:10.490 --> 01:17:12.460
given the present, okay?

01:17:12.460 --> 01:17:14.450
This is something that you can say.

01:17:14.450 --> 01:17:18.510
Condition predictability, is, I think,

01:17:18.510 --> 01:17:23.510
more about dependence as
opposed to independence.

01:17:24.150 --> 01:17:27.640
So, being independent or
conditionally independent,

01:17:27.640 --> 01:17:32.420
does not mean that the
