01:17:32.420 --> 01:17:35.200
So the mutual information
between the past,

01:17:35.200 --> 01:17:36.700
let's stick with this example,

01:17:36.700 --> 01:17:38.243
the past and the future,

01:17:41.260 --> 01:17:42.480
can be...

01:17:43.385 --> 01:17:45.200
So the amount of information

01:17:45.200 --> 01:17:47.030
that you can extract from the past,

01:17:47.030 --> 01:17:50.730
in order to predict
the future, can be low,

01:17:50.730 --> 01:17:52.130
even though...

01:17:55.848 --> 01:17:57.430
So that's an additional requirement.

01:17:57.430 --> 01:18:00.110
So, it's independent of the assumption

01:18:00.110 --> 01:18:01.500
that the past and the future

01:18:01.500 --> 01:18:04.030
are conditionally independent,
given the present.

01:18:04.030 --> 01:18:05.610
So you can keep this,

01:18:05.610 --> 01:18:07.210
this condition-independent statements,

01:18:07.210 --> 01:18:10.720
past and future being
conditionally independent,

01:18:10.720 --> 01:18:11.960
given the present,

01:18:11.960 --> 01:18:14.580
and tune the predictability up,

01:18:14.580 --> 01:18:16.610
by increasing the mutual information,

01:18:16.610 --> 01:18:18.109
and tune it down,
- Round, with (indistinct)

